# KNOWN GAP — a `Box[Trait]` collection's element type LOSES THE BOX at three
# separate boundaries, so the receiver reads back as `Deque[trait Speaker]` /
# `trait Speaker` instead of `Deque[Box[Speaker]]` / `Box[Speaker]`.
#
# THREE CELLS OF ONE FAMILY, each a different boundary; this file pins the
# first, the other two are recorded here because they discriminate it:
#
#   (1) THE READ SIDE (this file). `q.get(0).unwrap().speak()` on a
#       `Deque[Box[Speaker]]` builds and then FAILS TO LINK:
#         undefined reference to `int64_t__speak'
#       The element type collapsed to `int64_t`, so the method mangle is
#       computed against `int` rather than against the boxed trait. The
#       INDEX read `q[0].speak()` on the same collection WORKS — that is the
#       discriminator, and it is why this is the `.get()`-chain boundary and
#       not the collection itself.
#
#   (2) THE METHOD-LOOKUP SIDE. `q.push_back(Box.new(Robot("R2")))` is
#       `error[E_NoMethodFound]: no method `push_back` found on type
#       `Deque[trait Speaker]`` — the printed receiver type has already lost
#       the Box. `q.push(...)` on the identical receiver resolves and runs.
#
#   (3) THE INDEX-ASSIGN DESTINATION SIDE. `v[0] = ^b` with a named
#       `Box[Robot] b` into a `Vector[Box[Speaker]]` is
#       `error[E_TypeMismatch]: type mismatch: expected `trait Speaker`,
#       found `Box[Robot]`` — the destination element type lost the Box, so
#       the only spelling that reaches the lowering is the TEMP form.
#
# ⚠ ALL THREE ARE PRE-EXISTING AND UNCHANGED by R49 Track M2's trait-object
# pack fix, which is the WRITE side of a different axis (whether the pack
# fires at a consuming position). This family is the axis of what the element
# type IS by the time the typecheck and the mangler read it.
#
# ⚠ Payload is heap-forced through `mk`.
#
# INTENDED: prints `R2!`, rc 0, on both backends.
from std.collections import Box
from std.collections import Deque

trait Speaker:
    String speak(self)

struct Robot:
    String id

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String speak(self):
        return self.id + "!"

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Deque[Box[Speaker]] q = Deque[Box[Speaker]]()
    q.push(Box.new(Robot(mk("R", "2"))))
    print(q.get(0).unwrap().speak())
